course: dictionary
lesson: 12619
title: Fair or bored? Meeting disinterested
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disinterested means fair, because you gain nothing either way, so you do not take sides. Think of a referee: a referee who wants one team to win is not disinterested. «The referee was disinterested, so she gave the penalty to neither side.» The clue is fair decisions, not bored or sleepy.
explain: Use the context to check. «We asked a disinterested observer to count the votes, someone with no friends in either group.» An observer with no reason to pick a side is disinterested. Ask yourself: would a fair person act like this? If yes, the meaning fits.
explain: Be careful: some people use disinterested to mean bored or not interested, as in «He was disinterested in the film.» Many careful writers avoid this, because the main meaning is fair. For the careful meaning, use disinterested for fairness, and uninterested for not caring.
fact: Disinterested means fair, because you do not gain anything either way.
fact: «A disinterested judge» does not support one side.
fact: «Disinterested advice» comes from someone with nothing to win.
fact: Informal speech sometimes uses disinterested to mean not interested, but careful writers say uninterested instead.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in fair: if the sentence still makes sense, disinterested is probably right.
exercise: «The referee was disinterested, so she gave no advantage to either team.» What does disinterested mean here? | Very tall | Bored and sleepy | Angry with both teams | *Fair, not taking sides
exercise: «We wanted disinterested advice, so we asked someone with nothing to gain.» Which word has the same meaning as disinterested here? | noisy | hungry | tired | *fair
exercise: Ella wrote, «He was disinterested in the film.» Why might a careful writer change this word? | Because disinterested means hungry | Because disinterested means very loud | *Because disinterested means fair, while uninterested means not caring | Because the film was too long
test: «The judge was disinterested and gave the prize fairly.» What does disinterested mean? | Unfair and greedy | Asleep | Friendly | *Fair, with nothing to gain
test: «A disinterested observer can give honest advice.» Which person is most likely to be disinterested? | *A neutral stranger with no link to either team | The coach who wants her team to win | The player who scored the most goals | Her best friend
exam: Which sentence uses disinterested to mean fair? | «The disinterested dog slept all afternoon.» | *«The disinterested referee gave the penalty to neither side, after checking carefully.» | «My brother is disinterested, because he wants to win the prize.» | «The disinterested referee gave the penalty to her own friend.»
